WEBVTT

00:00:00.713 --> 00:00:01.758
Welcome to Prac360:

00:00:01.758 --> 00:00:04.784
the complete practice system for South African doctors.

00:00:04.784 --> 00:00:14.686
In the next few minutes we'll walk through a day in a practice, from the first booking to the payment from the medical aid, and show you how Prac360 takes the admin off your hands.

00:00:15.388 --> 00:00:17.079
Here's what we'll cover:

00:00:17.079 --> 00:00:32.020
the dashboard and front desk, the patient file, consultations with AI Scribe, billing and claims, payments and stock, the modules, Assist and Talk, the Prac360 network, and how your team stays safe and supported.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.827
Everyone signs in with their own login.

00:00:34.827 --> 00:00:42.769
Two-step verification adds a code from your phone, so your patients' information stays protected, and each person only sees what their role allows.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.876
The Home Dashboard is your morning briefing:

00:00:45.876 --> 00:00:52.932
turnover and collections this month, what medical aids and patients owe, today's appointments, and anything that needs attention.

00:00:55.471 --> 00:01:00.892
Messages from Prac360 appear right on the dashboard, and fold away when you've read them.

00:01:00.892 --> 00:01:06.251
Each person can arrange the dashboard their own way, and choose day, dusk or night mode.

00:01:08.472 --> 00:01:10.780
The diary is built for a busy front desk.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:18.323
Each doctor has a column, appointments show their status, and you change it with one click as the patient arrives, goes in and leaves.

00:01:21.673 --> 00:01:26.166
A red marker shows who was seen but not billed yet, so nothing slips through.

00:01:26.166 --> 00:01:31.768
No-shows are marked automatically, and the oncology treatment chairs sit right beside the diary.

00:01:32.873 --> 00:01:34.033
Booking takes seconds.

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:38.883
Choose the patient, and the doctor, time and length are filled in from the slot you clicked.

00:01:38.883 --> 00:01:41.361
Double bookings are stopped before they happen.

00:01:43.873 --> 00:01:48.636
Registering a new patient is one simple form, with compulsory fields clearly marked.

00:01:48.636 --> 00:01:51.414
The medical aid membership can be checked online.

00:01:56.078 --> 00:01:59.367
The patient file shows the whole patient on one screen:

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:05.586
medical aid, allergies, chronic medicines and conditions, visits, documents, the account and follow-ups.

00:02:08.278 --> 00:02:10.015
Some doctors like to type.

00:02:10.015 --> 00:02:13.289
The Classic consultation is a clean, simple note:

00:02:13.289 --> 00:02:19.302
history, examination, diagnosis and plan, with smart ICD-10 search and your own templates.

00:02:20.003 --> 00:02:21.498
Others prefer to talk.

00:02:21.498 --> 00:02:28.565
With AI Scribe, and only with the patient's permission, Prac360 listens and fills in the note as you go:

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:35.225
the complaint, the vital signs, the examination, the diagnosis with its ICD-10 code, and the plan.

00:02:40.205 --> 00:02:46.397
It linked the ICD-10 code by itself, and it learns from your choices, so there's less to check every time.

00:02:46.397 --> 00:02:48.734
It even works when the patient is quiet:

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.486
just say the details yourself.

00:02:52.406 --> 00:02:53.978
When you finish, you review.

00:02:53.978 --> 00:02:58.920
Anything that needs a second look is listed, and the fix button corrects it in one step.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.671
Nothing is signed or billed until you approve it.

00:03:06.607 --> 00:03:13.655
The follow-up manager keeps track of chronic patients, results to review and recalls, so nobody falls through the cracks.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:19.633
Signing the note creates the bill with the right tariff codes.

00:03:19.633 --> 00:03:27.833
Before anything is sent, Prac360 checks the codes, modifiers and ICD-10 rules, and the optional SAMA billing coach checks every line.

00:03:28.533 --> 00:03:31.157
Claims go to the medical aids electronically.

00:03:31.157 --> 00:03:34.773
On the awaiting payment list you see every claim's EDI status:

00:03:34.773 --> 00:03:40.254
sent, through the switch, accepted, and waiting for payment, with a warning when it's overdue.

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:46.248
If a claim is rejected, Prac360 explains why in plain language.

00:03:46.248 --> 00:03:47.466
Step one, fix it:

00:03:47.466 --> 00:03:51.622
for example the dependant code or an authorisation number.

00:03:51.622 --> 00:03:54.703
Step two, re-send it by EDI with one click.

00:03:57.935 --> 00:04:03.023
When the medical aid pays, the electronic remittance is imported and reconciled automatically.

00:04:03.023 --> 00:04:06.812
Short payments move to the patient's account, ready for the statement.

00:04:08.136 --> 00:04:11.478
Payments and accounts keep the money side simple:

00:04:11.478 --> 00:04:18.434
capture cash, card or EFT in seconds, print or email statements, and see the age analysis at a glance.

00:04:19.135 --> 00:04:24.641
Reports cover everything, from turnover and collections to rejections, debtors and stock:

00:04:24.641 --> 00:04:28.353
on screen, as PDF or Excel, or emailed to you automatically.

00:04:29.053 --> 00:04:37.517
With stock and dispensing, medicines are tracked by batch and expiry, you're warned when it's time to order, and dispensed items are billed straight from stock.

00:04:39.253 --> 00:04:47.287
For practices that admit patients, the hospital and wards module gives you a live ward board, admissions, authorisations, theatre and the hospital account.

00:04:49.457 --> 00:04:53.741
The oncology module follows the cancer patient from referral to follow-up:

00:04:53.741 --> 00:05:02.135
treatment plans and cycles, nursing and pharmacy checks, authorisations, and treatment chairs, where you put a patient in a chair with one click.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:06.854
Assist is like a personal assistant inside Prac360.

00:05:06.854 --> 00:05:08.983
Ask it anything in your own words:

00:05:08.983 --> 00:05:15.056
what do I need to do today, what allergies does Thandiwe have, or take me to the rejected claims.

00:05:16.661 --> 00:05:18.545
It also does the work for you.

00:05:18.545 --> 00:05:23.693
Tell it that a patient is allergic to aspirin, or to book Pieter on Friday at ten.

00:05:23.693 --> 00:05:26.205
If something is missing, it simply asks.

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:30.401
Or just talk.

00:05:30.401 --> 00:05:33.962
Talk is a real voice conversation, like talking to a colleague:

00:05:33.962 --> 00:05:38.935
Assist listens, answers out loud, and you can interrupt it at any time just by speaking.

00:05:38.935 --> 00:05:44.586
A small glowing circle shows it's listening, so the conversation never gets in the way of your work.

00:05:47.867 --> 00:05:49.543
Now, the Prac360 network.

00:05:49.543 --> 00:05:56.314
With the patient's consent, every Prac360 doctor who treats them works from one shared clinical file.

00:05:57.014 --> 00:06:02.744
Consent can be given at the practice, where reception reads a short, plain-language explanation.

00:06:02.744 --> 00:06:09.130
It covers all clinical records, including hospital admissions and oncology, but never accounts or payments.

00:06:11.718 --> 00:06:15.232
Or patients do it themselves in the Prac360 patient app.

00:06:15.232 --> 00:06:22.324
They see every record Prac360 holds on them, give consent with one tap, see who looked, and can stop at any time.

00:06:26.918 --> 00:06:34.026
Every doctor treating the patient now opens one combined, read-only file, with each entry marked by the practice that recorded it.

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:38.673
And patients can book any doctor in the network, straight into that practice's diary.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:46.037
Your team stays connected with internal messages:

00:06:46.037 --> 00:06:47.764
to everyone or to one person.

00:06:47.764 --> 00:06:51.752
They pop up to be acknowledged, but never interrupt a consultation.

00:06:52.454 --> 00:06:54.398
Found a problem or have an idea?

00:06:54.398 --> 00:06:56.342
Report it straight from Prac360.

00:06:56.342 --> 00:07:01.324
The Prac360 team sees it, can ask you questions, and lets you know when it's done.

00:07:02.025 --> 00:07:03.227
Training is built in.

00:07:03.227 --> 00:07:09.695
The Training Academy has short courses for every role, show me tours on the real screens, and a printable manual.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.813
What's new keeps everyone up to date.

00:07:13.028 --> 00:07:22.130
The practice manager controls who can do what, with roles for reception, nurses, doctors, billing and management, and every change is recorded in the audit trail.

00:07:23.228 --> 00:07:25.572
Every practice gets the core system.

00:07:25.572 --> 00:07:27.656
Then you add only what you need:

00:07:27.656 --> 00:07:37.033
Assist and AI Scribe, stock and dispensing, hospital and wards, oncology, dental, the SAMA billing coach, advanced reports and priority support.

00:07:37.734 --> 00:07:44.664
Your data is protected with personal logins, two-step verification, roles and a full audit trail.

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:47.308
And Prac360 is made for South Africa:

00:07:47.308 --> 00:07:51.451
medical aids, ICD-10, NAPPI codes, PMBs, VAT and the rand.

00:07:52.155 --> 00:07:52.659
Prac360.

00:07:52.659 --> 00:07:55.178
Less admin, more time for your patients.

00:07:55.178 --> 00:07:59.271
We'll set it up with your codes, your medical aids and your team.

00:07:59.271 --> 00:08:01.160
Book your personal demo today.

